# pod-curator proposal — REALIGNMENT, not yet applied (two-stage commit, D73).
# Intended landing spot on the Pod:
#   /vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/2026-05-24T11-47-31Z/catalog-meta-d77-description.ttl
# The curator PROPOSES; a human / higher-trust agent crystallizes.

<urn:uuid:2d6bcbbe-f4f8-484f-b21c-80c8a16733ee>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    # what gets corrected: the shape-catalog container metadata
    as:object </vault/meta/shapes/.meta> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    # ground-truth precedence: deployed Pod (the live 8 NodeShapes) + the decision that
    # superseded D77.
    prov:used </vault/meta/shapes/> ,
              <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem> ;  # vocab
    # the stale prior: a D77-era five-shape description string.
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/meta/shapes/.meta> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:SupersededConcept ;
    mem:rationale """The shape-catalog container .meta carries
dc:description "wiki-memory L3 SHACL shapes (D77). Five shapes: page, source, person,
procedure, working." — a retired D77-era statement. D98 (decisions.md:658) supersedes D77,
retiring the five-shape catalog: ProcedureShape -> wiki:HowToShape, SourceShape merged into
wiki:ConceptShape (source re-introduced 2026-05-23 only as a class-extension example, not a
core shape). The live catalog (GET /vault/meta/shapes/) holds the 8 D98 NodeShapes
(page, thing, concept, person, place, event, organization, howto) plus working/resource/
template and the addressbook + owner-identity overlay shapes (18 files total). The container
dc:modified is 2026-05-23 but the description text was never realigned. Repair direction is
prose -> reality. NOTE: the separate '8 vs 11 files' concern that triggered this audit is a
mem:FalsePositive — D98 says verbatim '8 SHACL NodeShapes (11 shape files total)', correct at
its granularity; no repair made to that count claim.""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-24T11:47:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

